From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 04:19:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09/36] fix(gastown): pass --include-infra on every patrol wisp
 query (gcp-xbl)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patrol wisp roots are ephemeral beads that live in the wisps table. bd's
list command sets filter.SkipWisps whenever --include-infra is absent and
the requested --type is not a configured infra type (cmd/bd/list.go:1097);
`molecule` never is, so every `gc bd list --type=molecule` query the witness,
refinery, and deacon prompts and patrol formulas ship returned zero rows —
silently, with no error to notice. Probed live against the gascity-packs
ledger: `--status=open --type=molecule` -> 0 results, the same query plus
--include-infra -> 1 result.

The consequences differ per agent but all leak. The witness reconcile-to-
exactly-one blocks saw an empty list, so they never burned a surplus wisp and
never resumed a queued one — each cycle poured a fresh wisp and stranded the
prior one. Refinery and deacon use the same query to resolve CURRENT_WISP when
GC_BEAD_ID is unset; it resolved empty, they took the "Could not resolve
current wisp; not burning" path, and the just-poured successor left the old
wisp behind. This commit adds --include-infra to all sixteen shipped molecule
queries, including the prose one in the refinery patrol-summary step.

The reconcile blocks carried a second defect: they queried --status=open only,
so a successor a crashed session had already flipped to in_progress was
invisible and leaked forever. Those now query --status=open,in_progress and
filter out the wisp the agent is on by id, so a claimed-but-orphaned wisp is
reconciled while the live one can never be burned out from under the agent.
That exclusion is why the status widening is safe, and why the witness formula's
next-iteration step now resolves CURRENT_WISP explicitly instead of burning a
hand-substituted <this-wisp-id> placeholder. The deacon prompt's fallback gains
the surplus burn the witness already had, so all three agents reconcile alike.

Validation: tests/test_wisp_molecule_queries.py is a new static guard in the
style of test_no_bare_bd_commands.py — it walks tracked files, joins shell line
continuations, and fails any --type=molecule flag not paired with
--include-infra, with detector self-tests for the space form, the continuation
form, and the `issue_type=molecule` prose spelling it must not flag. Verified
red against the pre-fix tree (17 sites reported) and green after. Full suite:
103 passed / 7 skipped; golangci-lint 0 issues; validate_registry.py ok;
go vet, go build, go test -race all clean.

Follow-up: tests/test_gc_role_prompt_integration.py has one failure when run
with GC_TEST_BIN set (claim route mismatch). It reproduces on a clean
origin/integration checkout and is unrelated to this change; filed as gcp-7af.

Both static guards also learned to skip patches/, the derived format-patch
export. Its hunks quote the pre-image of every changed line, so this commit's
own export re-introduced the broken query text and a removed bare-bd line, and
the guards flagged their own fix — a structural gap in the fork patch system
that only shows up once a fork commit deletes a guarded pattern. Skipping the
derived artifact costs no coverage: the shipped post-image of that content is
still scanned directly.
